    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is headlined by **Josh Naylor** (68.45) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.21), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Nick Martinez and Cal Quantrill, respectively. **Josh Naylor** remains a primary anchor, with his 19% boost from the opposing SP skill and a dynamic platoon advantage pushing his efficiency well above his base projection. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** earns a top-tier slot because of the favorable SP xERA of 4.79 and a 6% boost for batting third. While **Corbin Carroll** (67.48) continues to provide a high floor even without a confirmed lineup, **Seiya Suzuki** (64.86) rounds out our strongest group; despite a 35% rain risk in his matchup against Hunter Greene, his strong park factors and SP skill advantage keep him as an elite play.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's board was keeping **Austin Riley** (57.16) on the bench. He nearly unseated **Travis Bazzana** (57.03) or **Jose Caballero** (59.91), but the optimizer ultimately prioritized **Jose Caballero** due to his unique combination of a 13% dynamic platoon boost against a left-handed pitcher and the vital opportunity for stolen bases against a slow-delivering pitcher. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (62.51) and **Kyle Karros** (63.20) are high-variance starts against Robbie Ray; the 19% boost from Ray's high xERA and favorable winds blowing out provide a ceiling that makes them preferable to the safer but lower-upside profile of **Brice Turang** or **Zach McKinstry** sitting on the bench. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely for **Seiya Suzuki**, as any delay could necessitate a pivot to **Austin Riley**. Additionally, because several players including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Kyle Karros** are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" owners should remain agile. The high-risk nature of starting **Mickey 